From 93820aef5a89e40f14cc4ac34663c630ee9522d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 05:36:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Smoothers and adaptive tolerance: review (scaling invariance,
 first choice)

- OperatorSmoothersTest: the Jacobi and Chebyshev smoothers are checked
  to be invariant by a symmetric diagonal scaling of the operator (same
  numbers of iterations of the conjugate gradient), the scaled system
  being solved by the linear solver of the unscaled one: a smoother which
  ignores the diagonal, or which is not set up again for a new operator,
  is detected.
- AdaptiveLinearSolverTolerance: without the norm of the residual of the
  previous linear solve, the first choice uses the formula of the second
  one for this iteration (instead of a null norm); unit tests of the
  independence of the first choice on gamma and of this fallback.
- Glossary: differences with MFEM, bound against oversolving, tolerance
  lower than the one of the linear solver, cost of the power method.
- The tests of the linear solvers without behaviours are declared outside
  the tests requiring TFEL.
